## Description

This project demonstrates the basic concepts of JavaScript, including objects, arrays, arrays of objects, classes, loops, conditional statements, and object-oriented programming.

The program runs in the browser console and uses `console.log()` to display the output.

## Features

- Creates and manipulates JavaScript objects.
- Creates and displays arrays.
- Loops through arrays.
- Creates an array of student objects.
- Determines whether students have passed or failed.
- Implements a Student class.
- Uses methods to introduce students and check their results.

## Technologies Used

- JavaScript (ES6)

## Project Structure

```
project-folder/
│── script.js
│── README.md
```

## How to Run

1. Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
2. Open `script.js`.
3. Open the browser Developer Tools (F12).
4. Select the **Console** tab.
5. Run the program using Live Server or execute the file in the browser.
6. View the output in the console.

## Concepts Covered

- Variables
- Objects
- Arrays
- Arrays of Objects
- Loops
- Conditional Statements
- Classes
- Methods
- Functions
- Object-Oriented Programming

